    "title": "Thursday of the 28th Week in Ordinary Time",
    "text": "The readings today are about the wideness of God’s mercy. Dear brothers and sisters in Christ, in our first reading Saint Paul, writing to the Romans, speaks to a mixed community — some born Jewish, others Gentile. His task is delicate: to remind them that Christians remain heirs of God’s promises to Abraham, yet are no longer bound by the old Law. Both Jew and Gentile, he says, have failed to keep God’s commandments, but both can be saved — not by their own goodness, but by faith in the God who longs to save. Read more at https://sj.mcharlesworth.fr/\nPrevious",
